Dialogue: 3,0:07:45.74,0:07:51.49,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}SUBMARINE CREW AT WORK · USS SKATE
Dialogue: 0,0:08:05.13,0:08:07.66,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Seadragon went on with her war patrol.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:07.68,0:08:10.81,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}On October 10, she sank the Japanese cargo ship
Dialogue: 0,0:08:10.83,0:08:14.44,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Shigitre Maru, 47 seconds after the first torpedo hit.
Dialogue: 2,0:08:05.38,0:08:11.13,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 974 0 l 974 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:08:05.38,0:08:11.13,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:08:05.38,0:08:11.13,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}ARCHIVAL FILM · 1945 · U.S. NAVY · NOT SEADRAGON
Dialogue: 3,0:08:05.38,0:08:11.13,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}PERISCOPE SHEARS OF A U.S. FLEET SUBMARINE
Dialogue: 0,0:08:14.91,0:08:16.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}She kept fighting.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:16.03,0:08:19.21,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}On September 22 she attacked a cruiser, and missed.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:19.23,0:08:22.40,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}On September 30, a surface attack damaged a ship in
Dialogue: 0,0:08:22.42,0:08:22.96,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}a convoy.
Dialogue: 2,0:08:15.16,0:08:20.91,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 867 0 l 867 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:08:15.16,0:08:20.91,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:08:15.16,0:08:20.91,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}ARCHIVAL FILM · 1945 · U.S. NAVY · NOT SEADRAGON
Dialogue: 3,0:08:15.16,0:08:20.91,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}A U.S. FLEET SUBMARINE ON THE SURFACE
Dialogue: 0,0:08:23.43,0:08:27.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}She came back to port about six weeks after the operation.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:27.03,0:08:30.04,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}The squadron medical officer examined the patient
Dialogue: 0,0:08:30.06,0:08:31.90,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}and found a firm, healed scar.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:31.92,0:08:34.93,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}His conclusion, as the Navy's historians tell it:
Dialogue: 0,0:08:34.95,0:08:38.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Lipes and his shipmates had saved the young man's life.
Dialogue: 2,0:08:23.68,0:08:29.43,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 867 0 l 867 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:08:23.68,0:08:29.43,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:08:23.68,0:08:29.43,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}ARCHIVAL FILM · 1945 · U.S. NAVY · NOT SEADRAGON
Dialogue: 3,0:08:23.68,0:08:29.43,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}A U.S. FLEET SUBMARINE ON THE SURFACE
Dialogue: 0,0:09:06.77,0:09:09.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}After the patrol, a war correspondent named George
Dialogue: 0,0:09:09.85,0:09:13.09,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Weller met Lipes aboard the submarine tender Holland.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:13.11,0:09:15.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Weller wrote for the Chicago Daily News.
Dialogue: 2,0:09:07.02,0:09:12.77,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 837 0 l 837 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:09:07.02,0:09:12.77,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:09:07.02,0:09:12.77,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}ARCHIVAL FILM · 1945 · U.S. NAVY · NOT SEADRAGON
Dialogue: 3,0:09:07.02,0:09:12.77,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}A U.S. FLEET SUBMARINE GOES UNDER
Dialogue: 0,0:09:16.02,0:09:19.26,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Lipes himself was back in the United States by
Dialogue: 0,0:09:19.28,0:09:20.18,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}January 1943.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:20.20,0:09:24.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}By then, his name was in newspapers across the country.
Dialogue: 2,0:09:16.27,0:09:22.02,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 837 0 l 837 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:09:16.27,0:09:22.02,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:09:16.27,0:09:22.02,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}ARCHIVAL FILM · 1945 · U.S. NAVY · NOT SEADRAGON
Dialogue: 3,0:09:16.27,0:09:22.02,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}A LONE SUBMARINE ON AN EMPTY SEA
Dialogue: 0,0:09:46.53,0:09:48.08,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Hollywood noticed too.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:48.10,0:09:51.58,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}The submarine film Destination Tokyo, released in
Dialogue: 0,0:09:51.60,0:09:55.72,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}1943 with Cary Grant, borrowed the operation for its plot.
Dialogue: 2,0:09:46.78,0:09:52.53,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 837 0 l 837 132 l 0 132{\p0}
