Dialogue: 3,0:12:22.50,0:12:27.00,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}TODAY: USS WASHINGTON LEAVES DRY DOCK
Dialogue: 0,0:12:27.05,0:12:30.58,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}From 1959 into the 1970s, the big missile submarines
Dialogue: 0,0:12:30.60,0:12:32.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}did carry physicians.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:32.03,0:12:35.56,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Each of their two crews, Blue and Gold, had a doctor
Dialogue: 0,0:12:35.58,0:12:37.82,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}and an independent duty corpsman.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:37.84,0:12:41.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Even then, according to a Navy medicine historian,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:41.25,0:12:44.78,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}the corpsmen handled most of the daily medical care.
Dialogue: 2,0:12:27.30,0:12:33.05,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 953 0 l 953 132 l 0 132{\p0}
